@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+Zahir Uddin is an enterprise IT executive with more than 25 years leading technology strategy, infrastructure, cybersecurity, and data governance across biotechnology, pharmaceutical, and other regulated industries. He most recently served as Head of IT (CIO-equivalent) at SK Life Science, Inc., where he built the enterprise IT organization that carried the company from pre-commercial status through its first U.S. product launch and on to $1B in annual commercial operations - an arc that closely mirrors the stage MBX Biosciences is now entering.
+
+At SK Life Science, Zahir set and executed enterprise IT strategy spanning cloud infrastructure, enterprise applications, cybersecurity, and AI-enabled analytics, aligning an $8M technology budget with priorities across R&D, commercial, Finance, Quality, and Supply Chain. He reduced technology operating expenses by 30% through vendor renegotiation, cloud rightsizing, and license consolidation, while maintaining zero missed service-level agreements. He directed a cybersecurity program aligned to SOC 2 and NIST framework controls, and built practical AI capability in a GxP-regulated environment - including security operations automation and a next-best-action model for Medical Science Liaisons - always with validated systems remaining the system of record and human review before any action.
+
+Earlier at SK Life Science he led the transition from fragmented manual processes to an integrated, validated enterprise application ecosystem, enabling the company's first U.S. pharmaceutical launch within 14 months, and before that built the enterprise IT function from the ground up for the newly established U.S. entity. His prior career spans consulting and technology leadership roles at Reltio, Streebo, Univision, Project Performance Corporation, and Kalido, working with pharmaceutical clients including Eisai, AbbVie, Johnson & Johnson, GSK, Abbott, and Pfizer.
+
+He holds a Bachelor of Science in Information Systems with an Artificial Intelligence major (Honours) from Brunel University London, and is based in Montville, NJ, with willingness to relocate to the Burlington, MA area.